<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/julius-caesar.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/september-23">23 September</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The future Emperor Augustus is born in Rome</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Gaius Octavius was born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, great-nephew of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a>. As Augustus he ended the civil wars and turned the Republic into a monarchy that lasted for centuries.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-5">5 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The Senate condemns Catiline's fellow conspirators</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cicero">Cicero</a>'s fourth speech against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catiline">Catiline</a>, and Cato's demand for severity, the Senate voted to execute five conspirators without trial. Cicero was hailed as saviour of the Republic but later exiled for it.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/roman-annexation-of-syria">Roman annexation of Syria</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Roman annexation of Syria took place in 63 BCE, when the Roman general Pompey deposed the last Seleucid rulers and organised Syria as a Roman province.</p></div></li></ol></section>
